IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Defence Forces Retirement Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1967 (Cth).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1967A00091.txt. Commenced on Royal
-- Assent, 8 November 1967 (the commencing date). Seat: the pensioner or widow.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `DFRB 1967 class` IS ONE OF
    `a pensioner under s 4`
    -- s 10: but for s 53A of the 1948 Act, an eligible pensioner
    `a pensioner whose suspended pension again becomes payable (s 10)`
    -- s 7, s 9: the Finance Minister determines the rate
    `a pensioner under s 7`
    `a widow under s 8`
    `a widow under s 9`

-- s 5: why the pension payable is less than it would otherwise be.
DECLARE `Reduction` IS ONE OF
    `no commutation or election`
    `commuted under s 74 of the 1948 Act`
    `an election under s 61A or 61B of the 1963-1965 Act`

DECLARE `DFRB 1967 case` HAS
    `class`                                             IS A `DFRB 1967 class`
    -- s 3 eligible pensioner (for a widow, her husband's)
    `the pension began to be payable on`                IS A DATE
    -- s 3 definitions (for a widow, her husband's figures)
    `pension at current rate`                           IS A NUMBER
    `actual pension entitlement`                        IS A NUMBER
    `basic pension entitlement`                         IS A NUMBER
    -- s 5
    `reduction`                                         IS A `Reduction`
    `rate payable before the commencing date`           IS A NUMBER
    `rate without the commutation or election`          IS A NUMBER
    -- s 6: an increase under the 1961 Act or Part III of the 1963 Act
    `earlier increase`                                  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 8(2)
    `the one-half election applies`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 13
    `also entitled to a pension under the Superannuation Act 1922-1967` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 3 eligible pensioner: a pension "that commenced to be payable before the
-- thirtieth day of June, One thousand nine hundred and sixty-seven".
@ref s 3 eligible pensioner
GIVEN c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension is old enough` c IF
    c's `the pension began to be payable on` LESS THAN Date 30 6 1967

-- s 4: five-sevenths of the difference between the pension at current rate
-- and the basic pension entitlement, where the current rate exceeds the
-- actual entitlement.
@ref s 4
GIVEN c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 4 increase for` c MEANS
    IF c's `pension at current rate` GREATER THAN c's `actual pension entitlement`
    THEN 5/7 TIMES (c's `pension at current rate` MINUS c's `basic pension entitlement`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 5(1): scaled by the rate payable over the rate without the commutation or
-- election. s 8(1): for a widow, disregarded so far as it applies because of
-- a commutation under s 74 (an election still scales).
@ref ss 5, 8(1)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`, widow IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled` x `for` c `as widow` widow MEANS
    IF     c's `reduction` EQUALS `no commutation or election`
        OR (widow AND c's `reduction` EQUALS `commuted under s 74 of the 1948 Act`)
        OR NOT (c's `rate without the commutation or election` GREATER THAN 0)
    THEN x
    ELSE x TIMES c's `rate payable before the commencing date` DIVIDED BY c's `rate without the commutation or election`

-- s 6: reduced by the earlier increase, not below nil.
@ref s 6
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`less the earlier increase` x `for` c MEANS
    IF x MINUS c's `earlier increase` GREATER THAN 0 THEN x MINUS c's `earlier increase` ELSE 0

GIVEN c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`, widow IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increase under ss 4-6 for` c `as widow` widow MEANS
    `less the earlier increase` (`scaled` (`the s 4 increase for` c) `for` c `as widow` widow) `for` c

@ref ss 3-10, 13
@export default The increase in my DFRB pension under the Defence Forces Retirement Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1967 (Cth), for a pension that began before 30 June 1967: five-sevenths of the difference between my pension at current rate and my basic pension entitlement, where the current rate exceeds my actual entitlement (s 4), scaled down if I commuted part of my pension or made an election (s 5), less any increase under the 1961 Act or the 1963 Act (s 6); nil if I was also entitled to a Superannuation Act 1922 pension (s 13); for a widow, five-eighths (or one-half after the husband's election) of her husband's increase, without scaling for commutation (s 8); the same for a suspended pension when it resumes (s 10). NOTHING where the Finance Minister determines the rate (ss 7, 9). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `DFRB 1967 case`  @desc The class and the pension figures (the husband's, for a widow)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my 1967 increase for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (c's `class` EQUALS `a pensioner under s 7`) OR (c's `class` EQUALS `a widow under s 9`)
            THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the pension is old enough` c)
            THEN JUST 0
        IF c's `class` EQUALS `a widow under s 8`
            THEN IF c's `the one-half election applies`
                 THEN JUST (1/2 TIMES `the increase under ss 4-6 for` c `as widow` TRUE)
                 ELSE JUST (5/8 TIMES `the increase under ss 4-6 for` c `as widow` TRUE)
        IF c's `also entitled to a pension under the Superannuation Act 1922-1967`
            THEN JUST 0
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the increase under ss 4-6 for` c `as widow` FALSE)
